  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballymena Urban Council, January 1926. After the withdrawals of 6 January there was no contest in any of the three wards and all fifteen members were returned unopposed. Nine were nominated; Messrs. James Clarke, James Watt, Samuel Alexander and Walter Henry withdrew on 6 January, leaving five for five seats and no contest. Returned unopposed."
